{"id":"n1-192","title":"～といえども","romaji":"〜to iedomo","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Even if it is said that; Even though; Although.","longExplanation":"The ～といえども grammar point is used to show a contrast or contradiction. It is similar to 'even though' or 'although' in English. It can be used with nouns, verbs, adjectives, etc., to emphasize that the reality is different from the assumption or label.","formation":"Noun + といえども / Verb-plain form + といえども / Adjective + といえども","examples":[{"jp":"彼が天才といえども、ミスをすることはあります。","romaji":"Kare ga tensai to iedomo, misu o suru koto wa arimasu.","en":"Even though he’s a genius, he still makes mistakes.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"天才","vocabId":"1439090","reading":"てんさい"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いえ","vocabId":"1191730","reading":"いえ","baseForm":"いう"},{"surface":"ども","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ミス","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"する","vocabId":"1595910","reading":"する"},{"surface":"こと","vocabId":"1313580","reading":"こと"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あり","vocabId":"1225940","reading":"あり","baseForm":"ある"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3,4,5]},{"jp":"このパソコンが新しいといえども、問題があります。","romaji":"Kono pasokon ga atarashii to iedomo, mondai ga arimasu.","en":"Even though this computer is new, it has problems.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"パソコン","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"新しい","vocabId":"1361490","reading":"あたらしい"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いえ","vocabId":"1191730","reading":"いえ","baseForm":"いう"},{"surface":"ども","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"問題","vocabId":"1536010","reading":"もんだい"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あり","vocabId":"1225940","reading":"あり","baseForm":"ある"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。",